    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IAtr">I Atr</ref> 4.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="220" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he ðonne borh næbbe, slea mon hine ⁊ on ful lecge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="220" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IAtr_4-1.lnote.oe.5"/> he ðonne borh næbbe, slea man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IAtr_4-1.lnote.oe.9"/> hine ⁊ hine on ful lecge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="221" ed="#liebermann"/>Si tunc plegium non habeat, occidatur et cum dampnatis inhumetur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="54" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf he ðonne borh næbbe, slea man hine ⁊ hine<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IAtr_4-1.robnote.fn.5"/> on ful lecge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="221" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er aber keine Bürgschaft erhält, so tödte man ihn, und lege<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IAtr_4-1.lnote.de.1"/> ihn in schimpfliches [Grab].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he gets no surety, let him be killed and laid in a dishonoured [grave].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="55" ed="#robertson"/>If he has no surety, he shall be slain and buried in unconsecrated ground<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IAtr_4-1.robnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_33-1">II Cn 33.1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_4-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">220</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_4-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">220</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IAtr_4-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">148</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘strecke ihn als schuldig nieder’ [Schmid], was Tautologie wäre, auch heisst ‘<hi rend="italic">on</hi>’ nicht ‘als’, noch ist <hi rend="italic">ful</hi> acc. masc. Ein Sbst. ‘Schande’ versteht auch Toller, nimmt aber Feminina <hi rend="italic">ful</hi> und (um <hi rend="italic">on fulan</hi> II Cn 33, 1 zu erklären) <hi rend="italic">fule</hi> nach -<hi rend="italic">n</hi> Decl. an. Mir scheint hier Neutrum vorzuliegen, bei Cnut aber dt pl.; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb: ful</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Grab 2a C</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘strike him down as guilty’ [Schmid], which would be a tautology; moreover ‘<hi rend="italic">on</hi>’ does not mean ‘as’, nor is <hi rend="italic">ful</hi> acc. masc. Toller too understands a noun ‘shame’, but assumes feminines <hi rend="italic">ful</hi> and (to explain <hi rend="italic">on fulan</hi> II Cn 33, 1) <hi rend="italic">fule</hi> of the -<hi rend="italic">n</hi> decl. To me it seems that we have a neuter here, but in Cnut a dat. pl.; <hi rend="italic">see Wb: ful</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Grab 2a C</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IAtr_4-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With <hi rend="italic">on ful</hi> (acc. sing. neut.) cf. <hi rend="italic">on fulan</hi>, II Cn. 33, 1, which Liebermann takes to be dat. pl. The parallel phrase <hi rend="italic">jaceat in ungildan æcere</hi> occurs in IV Atr. 4.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IAtr_4-1.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><label>hine</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
